    "title": "Describe an affected subject",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-bei-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe an affected subject",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put the affected participant first, then 被 and an informative action or result. The agent can be named or omitted. In colloquial contexts, 给 and 让 can also mark an affected passive event; distinguish them from ordinary giving or asking someone to act.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我的书被他拿走了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ de shū bèi tā ná zǒu le 。",
                "meaning": "My book was taken away by him.",
                "audio": "b078bbb9ab2a3518605bde96c3bfa5e3e049d18938bf01accc6a28f81b499d01"
              },
              {
                "text": "我的书被拿走了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ de shū bèi ná zǒu le 。",
                "meaning": "My book was taken away.",
                "audio": "ce7798bc45e051f9457e126df97fc4ea9ae59f5563c2ba6b92c46487dfca95ed"
              },
              {
                "text": "这本书给老师拿走了。",
                "pinyin": "zhè běn shū gěi lǎoshī ná zǒu le 。",
                "meaning": "This book was taken away by the teacher, colloquially.",
                "audio": "c1c638af37269d37d5318684c9fcd42212e19dcfd369954f974aea509a4a8950"
              },
              {
                "text": "这杯水让他喝完了。",
                "pinyin": "zhè bēi shuǐ ràng tā hē wán le 。",
                "meaning": "He drank all the water in this cup, with the cup of water as the affected topic.",
                "audio": "33bae51562713ff83f25111879f2c1a7f08bb8a8bea2e834a58634d0ec6cfd63"
              }
            ]
